---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Improve — fix what keeps you out of AI answers | OpenSight" description="OpenSight Improve audits your website and reads the answers that recommended somebody else, then gives you a ranked list of what to change — with the evidence behind each one." ogDescription="A ranked list of what to fix, backed by evidence, plus a full site checklist on every run. No scores, no grades.">
<main>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden pt-14 pb-20 md:pt-20 md:pb-24">
    <div class="grid-field pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="bg-line/70 pointer-events-none absolute -top-32 -right-40 size-[32rem] rounded-full blur-[110px]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="site-shell relative">
      <div class="grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr]">
        <div class="relative z-10">
          <span class="product-tag border-line text-pine mb-6 w-fit bg-white"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20V7"/><path d="m6 13 6-6 6 6"/></svg>Improve</span>
          <h1 class="display-title max-w-[15ch] text-[clamp(2.3rem,4.4vw,3.9rem)]">Fix what keeps you out of ChatGPT’s answers.</h1>
          <p class="text-moss mt-6 max-w-[34rem] text-[1.08rem] leading-relaxed md:text-[1.18rem]">Every week, OpenSight audits your website and reads the answers that recommended somebody else — then gives you a ranked list of what to change, with the evidence behind each one.</p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <a href="https://dashboard.opensight.app/signup" class="button-primary">See what to fix <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a href="/monitor/" class="button-ghost">See Monitor <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-moss mt-4 text-[0.84rem]">Included in the S$50/month plan, with Monitor.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-[620px]" aria-label="An OpenSight action card with its category, reach, explanation and steps.">
          <div class="noise border-line overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-white shadow-[0_35px_90px_-42px_rgba(28,25,23,.38)]">
            <div class="border-line flex items-center justify-between border-b bg-stone-100 px-5 py-3">
              <span class="stat-label">Next actions · 20 Jul</span>
              <span class="border-line rounded-full border bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[0.58rem]">RANKED</span>
            </div>

            <article class="border-line border-b p-5 sm:p-6">
              <div class="text-moss flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.58rem] tracking-wider uppercase">
                <span class="bg-pine rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-white">Blocking</span>
                <span class="bg-paper rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">Website access</span><span>·</span><span>Affects every answer</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-[1.12rem] leading-snug font-bold">Your services page tells crawlers not to index it.</h2>
              <p class="text-moss mt-2 text-[0.88rem] leading-relaxed">A <code class="font-mono text-[0.82em]">noindex</code> directive was found on 2 of the 6 pages read, including /services.</p>
              <div class="border-line mt-4 rounded-lg border bg-paper px-4 py-3 text-[0.82rem]">
                <p class="stat-label">Steps</p>
                <p class="mt-2">1. Remove the <code class="font-mono text-[0.82em]">robots</code> meta tag from /services and /team.</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="p-5 opacity-70 sm:p-6">
              <div class="text-moss flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.58rem] tracking-wider uppercase">
                <span class="bg-paper rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">Website content</span><span>·</span><span>Affects 6 answers</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-[1.12rem] leading-snug font-bold">Your site never mentions same-day emergency callouts.</h2>
              <p class="text-moss mt-2 text-[0.88rem] leading-relaxed">Answers that omitted you cited pages where a competitor states it plainly.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-line border-y bg-stone-100">
    <div class="site-shell py-24 md:py-32">
      <div class="reveal grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-20">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Where actions come from</p>
          <h2 class="section-title max-w-[13ch]">Built from your site and your answers.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-[42rem] lg:pt-10">
          <p class="font-display text-[1.35rem] leading-snug font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] md:text-[1.6rem]">Every action is specific to your business.</p>
          <p class="text-moss mt-5 text-lg">Improve reads two things that are yours alone: your website, and the answers where a customer was recommended somebody else. Nothing on the list comes from anywhere but those.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="reveal panel p-7 md:p-9">
          <p class="font-mono text-pine text-[0.66rem] tracking-wider uppercase">Your site</p>
          <h3 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl leading-tight font-bold tracking-tight">A full technical audit, run every week.</h3>
          <p class="text-moss mt-4">Whether an AI crawler can reach your pages, read them, and work out who and where you are. Every finding is a real state of your site, checked directly — and anything failing that has a fix becomes an action.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="reveal panel bg-white p-7 md:p-9">
          <p class="font-mono text-pine text-[0.66rem] tracking-wider uppercase">Your answers</p>
          <h3 class="font-display mt-8 text-2xl leading-tight font-bold tracking-tight">The pages that won the answers you lost.</h3>
          <p class="text-moss mt-4">When a source is cited across answers that omit you, OpenSight reads it. A directory you are missing from is a listing to get. A competitor’s page making a claim your site never makes is a content gap.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-shell py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="reveal max-w-[42rem]">
      <p class="eyebrow">Content gaps</p>
      <h2 class="section-title max-w-[16ch]">What they say. What you don’t.</h2>
      <p class="text-moss mt-6 text-lg">When a recommendation goes elsewhere over something your site never says, you should be able to check that for yourself. So Improve quotes both sides — their words, next to yours.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal panel mt-12 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="border-line flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[0.6rem] tracking-wider uppercase md:px-8">
        <span class="bg-paper text-pine rounded px-2 py-1">Website content</span><span class="text-moss">·</span><span class="text-moss">Affects 6 answers</span>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 md:p-8">
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight font-bold tracking-tight">Your site never states that root canal treatment is completed in a single visit.</h3>
        <p class="text-moss mt-3 max-w-[46rem]">Across answers that recommended another clinic, the cited pages each led with single-visit treatment. Your services page describes the procedure but not how many appointments it takes.</p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <p class="stat-label mb-3">What the cited pages said</p>
            <div class="grid gap-3">
              <figure class="quote-card m-0">
                <blockquote class="text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed">“Most root canals here are completed in a single 90-minute appointment.”</blockquote>
                <figcaption class="text-moss mt-3 font-mono text-[0.62rem]">CITED · COMPETITOR A · /root-canal</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure class="quote-card m-0">
                <blockquote class="text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed">“Single-visit endodontics for most cases, with same-week appointments.”</blockquote>
                <figcaption class="text-moss mt-3 font-mono text-[0.62rem]">CITED · COMPETITOR B · /services</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="stat-label mb-3">What your site says</p>
            <figure class="quote-card m-0 bg-white">
              <blockquote class="text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed">“We provide root canal treatment using modern rotary instrumentation and digital imaging.”</blockquote>
              <figcaption class="text-moss mt-3 font-mono text-[0.62rem]">YOUR SITE · /services</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="text-moss mt-3 text-[0.88rem]"><b class="text-ink">Covered, but not with the detail cited alongside.</b></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border-line mt-8 rounded-xl border bg-paper p-5">
          <p class="stat-label">What to do</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[0.96rem]">If single-visit treatment is something you offer, say so on the services page in those words, with the typical appointment length.</p>
          <p class="text-moss mt-4 text-[0.82rem] italic">Publish only what is true of your practice. OpenSight never asks you to copy a competitor or claim an outcome you cannot support.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-line border-y bg-stone-100">
    <div class="site-shell grid items-center gap-12 py-20 md:py-24 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Ready to hand off</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight font-bold tracking-[-0.03em] md:text-4xl">You don’t have to do the work yourself.</h2>
        <p class="text-moss mt-5">Most of these are website changes. Every action copies as plain text — the finding, the evidence, the steps and the sources it was read from — ready to send to whoever runs your site, or to paste straight into a coding agent. Nothing is added that is not on the card.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal border-line rounded-xl border bg-white p-5 font-mono text-[0.78rem] leading-relaxed md:p-6">
        <p class="text-moss"># Your services page tells crawlers not to index it</p>
        <p class="mt-2">**Category:** Website access · **Affects:** every answer</p>
        <p class="mt-2">## Steps</p>
        <p>1. Remove the `robots` meta tag from /services…</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-shell py-24 md:py-32" id="checklist">
    <div class="reveal flex flex-col justify-between gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-end">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The visibility checklist</p>
        <h2 class="section-title max-w-[16ch]">Every check, every run — including the ones you passed.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="text-moss max-w-[27rem]">The list of actions shows what to do next. The checklist shows everything that was examined — including what passed — with the exact evidence behind each verdict, in plain language.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="reveal panel p-6 md:p-7">
        <div class="border-line flex items-center justify-between border-b pb-4">
          <p class="font-display font-bold">Access</p>
          <span class="text-moss font-mono text-[0.65rem]">1 to fix</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-moss mt-4">Whether an AI crawler can reach your pages at all, and whether anything on your site is telling it to stay away.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="reveal panel p-6 md:p-7">
        <div class="border-line flex items-center justify-between border-b pb-4">
          <p class="font-display font-bold">Structure</p>
          <span class="text-moss font-mono text-[0.65rem]">2 to fix</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-moss mt-4">Whether the pages it does reach are laid out so a machine can find them and understand what each one is for.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="reveal panel p-6 md:p-7">
        <div class="border-line flex items-center justify-between border-b pb-4">
          <p class="font-display font-bold">Identity</p>
          <span class="text-moss font-mono text-[0.65rem]">3 to fix</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-moss mt-4">Whether your site states who you are, what you do and where you are in a form a model can read without guessing.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-pinedeep noise text-white">
    <div class="site-shell grid items-start gap-14 py-24 md:py-32 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-24">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="font-mono mb-4 text-[0.72rem] tracking-[0.16em] text-white/55 uppercase">What we will not claim</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(1.9rem,3.8vw,3.2rem)] leading-[1.05] font-bold tracking-[-0.035em]">No score. No grade. No credit we didn’t earn.</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[34rem] text-lg text-white/68">Whether a change moved a recommendation is a question nobody can answer honestly from one week of data, so Improve does not answer it. It will confirm that an issue is no longer found. It will never tell you that its advice caused your visibility to rise.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal grid gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.06] p-6 md:p-7">
          <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">Nothing is invented.</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-white/65">A passage is quoted back to you only if it genuinely appears on the page it is attributed to. Where your details are unknown, the wording stays conditional.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.06] p-6 md:p-7">
          <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">Done means done, until the evidence says otherwise.</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-white/65">Complete an action and it leaves the queue. If a later run finds the same problem, it reopens. Dismiss one and it stays dismissed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.06] p-6 md:p-7">
          <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">An empty queue says what it means.</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-white/65">“No actions found in the latest evidence” — not “your site is healthy”.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-shell py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="reveal border-line relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-white px-6 py-14 text-center shadow-[0_30px_80px_-50px_rgba(28,25,23,.35)] md:px-12 md:py-20">
      <div class="bg-line/70 pointer-events-none absolute -top-32 left-1/2 size-96 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full blur-[100px]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="relative">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with the evidence</p>
        <h2 class="section-title mx-auto max-w-[18ch]">Find out what is keeping you out of the answer.</h2>
        <p class="text-moss mx-auto mt-5 max-w-[34rem]">Your first site audit and your first list of actions arrive with your first <a href="/monitor/" class="text-pine underline underline-offset-4">monitoring</a> run — the same day you sign up.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="https://dashboard.opensight.app/signup" class="button-primary">See what to fix <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="/pricing/" class="button-ghost">See pricing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
